quran[18]{c,v,t}:
  71,11,"He will send clouds upon you with abundant rains,"
  71,12,"and He will help you with wealth and sons, provide you with gardens and bless you with rivers."
  71,13,"What is the matter with you that you do not hope for Allah with veneration,"
  71,14,while He has created you through (various) stages?
  71,15,Have you not seen how Allah has created the seven heavens in layers one above the other?
  71,16,And (how) He has placed the moon within them as a (reflected source of) light and made the sun a (light emitting radiant) lamp?
  71,17,Allah caused you to grow from the earth like (the growth of) a plant.*
  71,18,"Then He makes you return to this (earth), and He will bring you out (of it) again."
  71,19,"And Allah has made the earth a vast expanse for you,"
  71,20,so that you may travel through its broad ways.’
  71,21,"Nuh (Noah) said: ‘My Lord! They have disobeyed me, following those (rebellious elites) whose wealth and children have increased them in nothing but loss."
  71,22,They have devised a tremendous plan (to keep the people astray).
  71,23,They say: ‘Do not leave your gods at any cost. Do not abandon Wadd or Suwa‘ or Yaghuth or Ya‘uq or Nasr (all of these idols).’
  71,24,They have already led many (people) astray. So do not increase the wrongdoers except in error.’
  71,25,"Because of their evildoings, they were drowned and admitted into the Fire. So they did not find any helpers for themselves against Allah."
  71,26,And Nuh (Noah) said: ‘My Lord! Do not leave upon the earth any inhabitant from among the disbelievers.
  71,27,"If You leave them, they will certainly lead Your servants astray, and they will give birth only to vicious sinners (and) staunch disbelievers."
  71,28,"My Lord! Forgive me and my parents, and (forgive) whoever enters my house as a believer, and (all) the believing men and the believing women, and do not increase the wrongdoers except in destruction.’"
